+# Design mocks
+
+Saved out of a session scratchpad on **2026-08-10** so they survive a restart. These are the
+generators behind the mocks the CPO reviewed that day and since.
+
+⚠ **The browser pane cannot open `file://`** — it times out after 300s. Serve over HTTP and
+MEASURE; reading the stylesheet was wrong three times running.
+
+```
+python -m http.server 8899 --bind 127.0.0.1     # in this folder, backgrounded
+preview_start url http://127.0.0.1:8899/<file>.html
+```
+
+## The page surfaces (GitLab issues are the authority, these are the renderings)
+
+| Generator | Page | Issue | Check |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `gen_competitions.py` | `/{locale}/competitions/` — the index | **#54** | `python gen_competitions.py` + `prove_region_checks_fail.py` |
+| `gen_competition_hub.py` | `/{locale}/{slug}/` — one league | #47 | `check_competition_hub.py` |
+| `gen_matches.py` · `gen_home.py` · `gen_block_standard.py` | the "Next matches" block | #50 | `check_row_consistency.py` |
+| `gen_interaction.py` | the interaction standard | #52 | `scan_clickables.py` |
+
+Shared, imported by every surface — **do not re-implement**: `rows.py` (the match row + group
+head), `interaction.py` (every clickable affordance).
+
+**Proposed seed shapes** live beside the generators and are read by them, because `!27` needs a
+clean tree: `competition_types.proposed.csv` (the shipped seed + `scope`, `label_i18n_key`,
+`label_en`) and `confederations.proposed.csv` (new, 7 rows). Both are guarded against the shipped
+seed and against the registry's own documented enum, so a mock cannot be designed against a
+taxonomy that is not real.
+
+## Provenance is the contract (#58)
+
+Every element on a page design declares its source; **a value with no source is a named gap, never
+a typed value**. `gen_competitions.py` carries the table (`PROVENANCE`) and renders it under the
+mock, so the design and its provenance are one artifact.
+
+---
+
+## Home-page mocks — Top players, Top teams, composed home
+
+**In the repo since 2026-09-10** — CPO ruling, recorded in `.claude/task/escalations.log` under
+`2026-09-10 chore/design-mocks-into-the-repo`. The generators and checks are tracked; the HTML they
+render is not — it is build output, `.gitignore`d, and regenerated by running them.
+
+⚠ They lived outside the repo from 2026-08-10 until then, and it broke them. Versioned apart from
+the catalogue and the stylesheet they read, they drifted until every generator died on a path that
+no longer existed, the player metric ids were renamed underneath them, and two checks hardcoded a
+metric label the CPO had since changed. Anything that reads the repo has to version with the repo.
+
+## The design they render
+
+The approved design is recorded in **GitLab #40** (Top players) and **#41** (Top teams). Those
+issues are the authority; these scripts are how it was rendered. If the two ever disagree, the
+issues win.
+
+Both blocks: four boards, one metric per board, top 7, all ranked descending, no column-header row,
+a club crest per row, one column of boards.
+
+## Running them
+
+Run them from anywhere; each derives the repo root from its own location. They read
+`dbt_project/seeds/metric_catalogue.csv` and inline `site_v2/src/styles/system.css`, so now that
+they version with those files, the mocks genuinely cannot drift from the shipped design system or
+invent a metric label. ⚠ That sentence used to be here while the path pointed at
+`D:/Projects/fdp-product` — a directory with no `dbt_project/` in it — so the guarantee was false
+and every generator raised FileNotFoundError.
+
+```
+python gen_top_players.py     -> top_players_mock.html
+python gen_top_teams.py       -> top_teams_mock.html
+python gen_home.py            -> home_mock.html   (imports the two above)
+```
+
+Then the checks — each asserts the rules the design actually depends on, not just that a file was
+produced:
+
+```
+python check_players.py
+python check_teams.py
+python check_home.py
+python prove_check_fails.py   # proves the stacked-branch check goes RED on the real defect
+```
+
+## Why the checks exist in this shape
+
+Several were written after a defect got past the earlier ones:
+
+- **`prove_check_fails.py`** exists because a check that has only ever been seen green proves
+  nothing. It reconstructs the CSS that shipped the "Bayern MünchenBundesliga" bug and asserts the
+  check fails on it.
+- The container-query check selects the query **by content**, because the first `@container` in the
+  file is the value-column one — `re.search` matched the wrong block.
+- Label lookups key on **`(metric_id, entity)`**. Several ids carry both a team and a player row, so
+  keying on `metric_id` alone silently takes the wrong label; that is the exact bug `!27` fixed in
+  `export_metric_definitions_json.py`.
+- Sort order is checked against each metric's catalogue **`direction`**, so a lower-is-better metric
+  cannot be ranked descending without an explicit recorded ruling.
+
+## Not design tooling, but kept because they were expensive
+
+- `make_payload.py` — builds a JSON body for `glab api --input`. `--raw-field description=@file`
+  silently sends the *path*, not the file.
+- `scan_issue.py` — scans a fetched issue for stale terms, forcing UTF-8 both ways.
+- `check_handover.py` — size against the 16,000-character cap, NEXT numbering, duplicate lines, and
+  presence of key phrases **whitespace-collapsed** (a line-based match misses a phrase that wraps).
+- `section_sizes.py` — per-section character counts, for deciding what to trim.
+
+## Every number in the mocks is placeholder
+
+The player and team names are real; the values attached to them are invented and were never
+measured. Nothing here has been run against BigQuery.
